  "post_stream": {
    "posts": [
      {
        "id": 10955,
        "name": "PlatinumWarlock",
        "username": "PlatinumWarlock",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/platinumwarlock/{size}/1869_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-08-14T15:15:19.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I just got my box yesterday, and my wife and I played a skirmish (Bunker and Ambuscade vs. Tachyon and Baron Blade) in Insula Primalis. &nbsp;We understood that the Volcano creates lava--easy to understand. &nbsp;</p><p>However, we were much less clear about how Hazard tokens work in general. &nbsp;Do you take damage if you are&nbsp;<em>in</em> the lava or&nbsp;<em>adjacent</em> to the lava? &nbsp;What about other Hazard token usages? &nbsp;The rulebook wasn't very clear on these...</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:42:08.996Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 0.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 10952,
        "topic_slug": "explain-hazard-tokens-for-a-noob",
        "display_username": "PlatinumWarlock",
        "primary_group_name": null,
        "flair_name": null,
        "flair_url": null,
        "flair_bg_color": null,
        "flair_color": null,
        "flair_group_id": null,
        "badges_granted": [],
        "version": 1,
        "can_edit": false,
        "can_delete": false,
        "can_recover": false,
        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": true,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>I just got my box yesterday, and my wife and I played a skirmish (Bunker and Ambuscade vs. Tachyon and Baron Blade) in Insula Primalis. &nbsp;We understood that the Volcano creates lava--easy to understand. &nbsp;</p><p>However, we were much less clear about how Hazard tokens work in general. &nbsp;Do you take damage if you are&nbsp;<em>in</em> the lava or&nbsp;<em>adjacent</em> to the lava? &nbsp;What about other Hazard token usages? &nbsp;The rulebook wasn&#39;t very clear on these...</p>",
        "actions_summary": [],
        "moderator": false,
        "admin": false,
        "staff": false,
        "user_id": 3746,
        "hidden": false,
        "trust_level": 1,
        "deleted_at": null,
        "user_deleted": false,
        "edit_reason": null,
        "can_view_edit_history": true,
        "wiki": false,
        "can_accept_answer": false,
        "can_unaccept_answer": false,
        "accepted_answer": false,
        "topic_accepted_answer": false
      },
      {
        "id": 114599,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-08-14T15:25:25.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hazard spaces activate when you are on them.</p><p>Lava deals more damage if there is lava adjacent, but you still trigger it only when you are on the space.</p><p>Cards like Burning tornado and Turret Bot create hazard spaces around them, the radius tells you how far out the hazard spaces go.</p><p>Turret Bot creates Hazard spaces in a radius of 2, so 2 spaces in any direction from Turret Bot is a hazard Space.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>To sum up:</p><p>1. &nbsp;You have to be on a hazard space to trigger it.</p><p>2. &nbsp;Things that crate a hazard space will tell you how far out they create them with the radius.</p><p>Bonus: &nbsp;Objects that create hazard spaces still use Line of Sight to attack.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:46:33.248Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
