      {
        "id": 114600,
        "name": "Ronway",
        "username": "Ronway",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-08-14T15:31:49.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hazard Spaces immediately trigger&nbsp;anytime a target enters a Hazard Space. If a target ends their turn on a Hazard Space, the Hazard Space will then trigger.</p><p>So say Proletariat want to take out The Operative, but she currently has the Hidden Blade in play (at least I believe that is the one where she creates Hazard Spaces), she only has 1 HP left, to Proletariat is feeling that he can take The Operative out. He decides to move next to her, so he triggers the Hazard space, getting attacked for being there. Proletariat tries his attack, but The Operative manages to block all his dice (curse her and getting bonus to Defense for being so low on health). Proletariat decides to try again since it is Unlimited, but once again fails. Now that he has used all his actions it goes to the To Be Continued, since he is standing on a Hazard Space, he will then suffer the attack again.</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:46:33.325Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
